WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.815
The story of my code is an animal parade. When you click

2
00:00:03.815 --> 00:00:06.880
an animal, it moves. Each move uses a repeat.

3
00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:10.880
My code uses repeats in this part to make the kangaroo

4
00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:11.150
hop.

5
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.603
The repeat runs four times. Each time, it switches to

6
00:00:14.603 --> 00:00:17.472
the next costume, moves thirty steps, and waits a

7
00:00:17.472 --> 00:00:19.580
little, so it looks like four jumps.

8
00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:24.250
It also uses a repeat to make the grasshopper hop.

9
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.094
This one runs six times, because the grasshopper has six

10
00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:30.840
costumes. Each time, it moves fifteen steps.

11
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:35.260
And the bee flies in a circle when you click it.

12
00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:38.554
Each time through, it switches costume, moves twenty

13
00:00:38.554 --> 00:00:41.498
steps, and turns thirty degrees. It does that twelve

14
00:00:41.498 --> 00:00:44.555
times, and twelve times thirty is three hundred sixty,

15
00:00:44.555 --> 00:00:46.650
so it ends up right where it started.

16
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.154
One thing a student might struggle with is the bee. The

17
00:00:50.154 --> 00:00:53.022
repeat count times the turn has to add up to three

18
00:00:53.022 --> 00:00:56.119
hundred sixty. If it doesn't, the bee won't finish its

19
00:00:56.119 --> 00:00:56.520
circle.

